winex11: Leave the X event context before calling IDropTarget::Drop.

handle_xdnd_drop_event calls drag_drop_drop() synchronously from inside call_event_handler, with
thread_data->current_event still pointing at the XdndDrop ClientMessage. Illustrator 2026 opens the dropped document
inside IDropTarget::Drop and shows a modal dialog right there ("Missing Fonts", PDF import options, ...).
X11DRV_ProcessEvents forces mask = 0 while current_event is set ("don't process nested events"), so the dialog's
message loop never gets a single X event: no clicks, no keys, and XCheckIfEvent rescans the growing queue forever
(100% CPU on the main thread). The application is frozen until killed (public #43).

On Windows the drop reaches the target through its own message loop and nested modal loops inside Drop work normally.
Clear current_event around the drag_drop_drop() call and restore it afterwards; XdndFinished is still sent once Drop
returns. Contributed in #43.

Test: tests/dragdrop/dropdlg.c opens a MessageBox inside Drop; tests/dragdrop/run_dropdlg.sh drags a file onto it
from a GTK X11 source and presses Enter on the box (before: FAIL timeout, the box gets no input; after: PASS).

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -1578,10 +1578,19 @@
 
 static void handle_xdnd_drop_event( HWND hwnd, XClientMessageEvent *event )
 {
+    struct x11drv_thread_data *thread_data = x11drv_thread_data();
+    XEvent *prev_event = thread_data->current_event;
     XClientMessageEvent e;
     UINT effect;
 
+    /* IDropTarget::Drop may run a modal loop (e.g. a "Missing Fonts" dialog after opening
+     * the dropped file). While current_event is set, X11DRV_ProcessEvents processes no X
+     * events at all, so such a dialog would never receive input. On Windows the drop
+     * arrives through the target's message loop, where nested modal loops work, so
+     * leave the event context before calling into the application. */
+    thread_data->current_event = NULL;
     effect = drag_drop_drop( hwnd );
+    thread_data->current_event = prev_event;
     xdnd_tracking = 0;
 
     /* Tell the target we are finished. */
